Lane Warden Production Battle Slice
Build: P2-0.21.0
Design baseline: 1.7
Stable install scope: /lol-the-spire/lane-warden-prod-v0.10.4/
P2-0.21.0 Ironbound Gate: a visible Gatekeeper issues repeating Iron Edicts against the most advanced lane. Presence or completed works can protect it; missed Edicts damage defenses, and each broken Guard enrages the remaining lane.
Gatekeeper victory grants 260 Salvage plus a premium Relic and Act Growth reward packet. Its Last Stand costs two Embers and ends the act without the premium packet.
P2-0.20.0 Ashen Rift: spend one Ember for a deterministic hidden movement, Presence, or fieldwork boon, or preserve Embers and take 160 Salvage. The choice saves immediately and cannot be reversed.
P2-0.19.0 Broken Switchback: alternating fall lines force a Presence-versus-infrastructure decision. The Warden braces best; completed fieldworks can hold with reduced tempo while the Warden attacks elsewhere.
Act 1 progression is now continuous: Outer Approach → Split Causeway → Ruined Forge → Broken Switchback → Ashen Rift → Ironbound Gate.
Existing saves remain compatible. P2 Strategic Fieldworks, Living Lanes combat, deployment, reward packet structure, Reclamation, and normal Last Stand rules are preserved.
The 182%-height organic battlefield, proportional two-axis pinch zoom, vertical panning, cut-through movement, tactile cohort models, casualties, and post-breach flow remain active.
P2-0.15.1 delivery protections remain: explicit shell build marker, mixed-shell repair, stale-shell rejection, and build.json-last deployment discipline.
